                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b7dcde45-da46-47aa-91f7-8e2d26c4bfab",
                        "source_entry_id": "92aa9223-f515-3982-8f15-208493512a1d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b5d4657e-69ec-3d15-99a0-a85c18b43330",
                        "source_sense_description": "abwertend: Ersatz für etwas oder jemanden in Ermangelung einer besseren Alternative",
                        "target_lang_word": "stopgap",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "stopgap",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93c3e5f3-15be-3ef4-ab27-6ca80d9905a4",
                                        "entry_id": "0ec0960b-2586-393e-9076-7dc3410e62a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which stops up or fills a gap or hole."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d26261b-fe2a-4ae4-8cb2-93f079a97c07",
                                                "sense_id": "93c3e5f3-15be-3ef4-ab27-6ca80d9905a4",
                                                "text": "[A] bit of ink and paper which has long been an innocent wrapping or stop-gap may at last be laid open under the one pair of eyes which have knowledge enough to turn it into the opening of a catastrophe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5eb610c3-064d-399a-928e-d7b67930b10f",
                                        "entry_id": "0ec0960b-2586-393e-9076-7dc3410e62a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something spoken to fill up an uncomfortable pause in speech; a filled pause or filler."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "18c0e94a-8b62-305f-83c4-c0ad936a1595",
                                        "entry_id": "0ec0960b-2586-393e-9076-7dc3410e62a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short-term fix or temporary measure used until something better can be obtained; that which serves as an expedient in an emergency; a band-aid solution."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08ffc7c1-1ddd-499a-ae76-ee2c4837eef4",
                                                "sense_id": "18c0e94a-8b62-305f-83c4-c0ad936a1595",
                                                "text": "The small company used their old product with a few kludged enhancements as a stopgap until they could develop a new product."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee1f8ba7-bd5d-4fe5-9b86-40a727a6e094",
                                                "sense_id": "18c0e94a-8b62-305f-83c4-c0ad936a1595",
                                                "text": "Perhaps I shall be told that this wintry exhibition is a mere stopgap and makeshift, until a fresh supply of bright new paintings can be procured, and that it is ultra vires to obtain such for love or money before the merry month of May."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27d00607-bf1f-444f-b8f4-a47621084483",
                                                "sense_id": "18c0e94a-8b62-305f-83c4-c0ad936a1595",
                                                "text": "It is often argued that the HST saved BR's InterCity market. It was only ever intended as a stopgap, but it proved to be a winner."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "980b4c16-1f31-382d-90dc-dedc142cf798",
                                        "entry_id": "0ec0960b-2586-393e-9076-7dc3410e62a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short-term fix or temporary measure used until something better can be obtained; that which serves as an expedient in an emergency; a band-aid solution.",
                                            "A person appointed or hired to fill a position temporarily until a permanent appointment or hire can be made; a temp."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "specifically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c69a8460-81f4-411f-949d-1b36f566399b",
                                                "sense_id": "980b4c16-1f31-382d-90dc-dedc142cf798",
                                                "text": "As witness the following. Mr Strudwick, the regular master of the form, happened on one occasion to be away for a couple of days, and a stop-gap was put in in his place. The name of the stop-gap was Mr Somerville Smith. He and Farnie exchanged an unspoken declaration of war almost immediately."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "stopgap",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3052ad1a-e16b-328e-915e-9fd6d52b8e02",
                                        "entry_id": "1b28cf02-6114-31a9-9a55-faeba89f5843",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Short-term; temporary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fe3f93f-6b43-4224-b01a-f4bd9c1f8693",
                                                "sense_id": "3052ad1a-e16b-328e-915e-9fd6d52b8e02",
                                                "text": "They put a stopgap solution in place, but need something more permanent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f310e30-4ee5-3758-a6a7-70fd828f2b76",
                                        "entry_id": "1b28cf02-6114-31a9-9a55-faeba89f5843",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Filling a gap or pause."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "stopgap",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61cc2cef-dbe8-3808-9dd5-9126ea3f9dfc",
                                        "entry_id": "49d67dcc-a8f2-3430-8001-535141c47431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To stop up or fill (a physical gap or hole, or a hiatus)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5914266-c7b4-3aa7-82ca-21883df89aba",
                                        "entry_id": "49d67dcc-a8f2-3430-8001-535141c47431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use something as a short-term fix or temporary measure until a better alternative can be obtained."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0afa525b-cb57-30d8-8668-82a0e20d24fd",
                                        "entry_id": "49d67dcc-a8f2-3430-8001-535141c47431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use something as a short-term fix or temporary measure until a better alternative can be obtained.",
                                            "To work at a position temporarily until a permanent appointment or hire is made."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "specifically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "92d7acc7-6c80-47ab-8647-2b4d59d94e57",
                        "source_entry_id": "92aa9223-f515-3982-8f15-208493512a1d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b5d4657e-69ec-3d15-99a0-a85c18b43330",
                        "source_sense_description": "abwertend: Ersatz für etwas oder jemanden in Ermangelung einer besseren Alternative",
                        "target_lang_word": "fill-in",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fill-in",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "095d2fdd-ae27-3e42-8a6a-fbdb191fe580",
                                        "entry_id": "c77afaff-5d8e-3b7b-b7ce-0305752f0141",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A temporary replacement for another, especially at a job."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a75fccf-4885-4c9d-af93-64ac457eae68",
                                                "sense_id": "095d2fdd-ae27-3e42-8a6a-fbdb191fe580",
                                                "text": "He went in to the Calsag bar to wrangle two fill-ins for the Goldenhoys as ordered."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9343ba3-6472-4108-8650-bdaf5d74f808",
                                                "sense_id": "095d2fdd-ae27-3e42-8a6a-fbdb191fe580",
                                                "text": "I was a fill-in. What that meant was you rode with each salesperson to learn his route, and then you could actually run his route when he was off or on vacation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6bb6cbe-96e9-32f9-968e-c7af5ece68fe",
                                        "entry_id": "c77afaff-5d8e-3b7b-b7ce-0305752f0141",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A substitution."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39613be3-d331-48e3-a973-68c848525e1e",
                                                "sense_id": "a6bb6cbe-96e9-32f9-968e-c7af5ece68fe",
                                                "text": "All our language is loose: whatever one means to say, all words are fill-ins for other words - as any cursory glance at a dictionary reveals."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bdac5dee-c196-3a20-8023-287136f9da6c",
                                        "entry_id": "c77afaff-5d8e-3b7b-b7ce-0305752f0141",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An intermediate result that must be stored temporarily during the course of a sparse matrix computation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa78a9e4-2896-4946-a378-80e0ba46bd1f",
                                                "sense_id": "bdac5dee-c196-3a20-8023-287136f9da6c",
                                                "text": "When a fill-in, aᵢⱼ⁽ˢ⁾ is created in the course of the computation, it may be necessary to make copies of the contents of certain parts of the ALU and CNLU at the ends of these arrays."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d8d497b-3abb-4962-b1c2-8b0f4e32bb35",
                                                "sense_id": "bdac5dee-c196-3a20-8023-287136f9da6c",
                                                "text": "In practice they are very sparse and generate few fill-ins in the remaining columns."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d02cbf9-f48e-4142-a333-47c0561280df",
                                                "sense_id": "bdac5dee-c196-3a20-8023-287136f9da6c",
                                                "text": "Suppose that there were no fill-ins added in the course of factorization. (This is unrealistic, but we have developed techniques to minimize the number of fill-ins and in practice the number of fill-ins may be relatively small.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4089d5a-9951-36f5-97fe-6e1be57131ab",
                                        "entry_id": "c77afaff-5d8e-3b7b-b7ce-0305752f0141",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A question or puzzle in which one is expected to fill in a missing part of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e28e21fe-0865-4a1f-879b-77f8b5b8596a",
                                                "sense_id": "b4089d5a-9951-36f5-97fe-6e1be57131ab",
                                                "text": "The main interaction styles supported by Web systems are direct manipulation, menus and form fill-ins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d04929c-c6fb-485c-b87b-1932993288a7",
                                                "sense_id": "b4089d5a-9951-36f5-97fe-6e1be57131ab",
                                                "text": "This part tests your writing skills in Spanish, and it consists of three different exercises: paragraph fill-ins, discrete sentence fill-ins, and an essay."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23075a68-94ef-40ab-993b-d647f8c69efd",
                                                "sense_id": "b4089d5a-9951-36f5-97fe-6e1be57131ab",
                                                "text": "I would pick three or four activities each day from a list of: oral reading, silent reading, filmstrips on the text book subject, short quizzes, chapter tests, semester exams, quarter exams, review sheets, \"find the word\" puzzles, research papers with library visits, lectures, debates (about four times a year), phonograph records from the library downtown for the music of the time era we were studying, movies, field trips, spelling lists, match the date with the name lists, timelines, map fill-ins, etc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7897c328-3105-493f-b0da-e2cdd902fcbd",
                                                "sense_id": "b4089d5a-9951-36f5-97fe-6e1be57131ab",
                                                "text": "This is truly a word fill-in book like no other."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "acf2e9ea-4d6a-3f82-bfc6-e6f7f488349c",
                                        "entry_id": "c77afaff-5d8e-3b7b-b7ce-0305752f0141",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A musical embellishment (usually percussion) that is added to connect musical phrases."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b15e5265-3b43-4343-90ce-200c654ce6e9",
                                                "sense_id": "acf2e9ea-4d6a-3f82-bfc6-e6f7f488349c",
                                                "text": "The following abbreviations are used for all drum solos and fill-ins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cbb40ca-893a-42df-ae55-2e3f695beda0",
                                                "sense_id": "acf2e9ea-4d6a-3f82-bfc6-e6f7f488349c",
                                                "text": "Fill-ins usually happen at the end of a four or eight-measure musical phrase."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "334be1c7-4ec7-3462-8ee6-0f63b218b18f",
                                        "entry_id": "c77afaff-5d8e-3b7b-b7ce-0305752f0141",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something added to fill a gap."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3244040a-b758-4520-82c0-1d97146a8e75",
                                                "sense_id": "334be1c7-4ec7-3462-8ee6-0f63b218b18f",
                                                "text": "With too many fill-ins the statistical results become dubious."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe3bafa5-d146-499d-b7b0-98525ed7ba12",
                                                "sense_id": "334be1c7-4ec7-3462-8ee6-0f63b218b18f",
                                                "text": "Originally, we'd planned a Basie-type thing, using lots of open rhythm, only without any piano for fill-ins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bda1a805-6449-43d3-8c81-7aa6e2623a37",
                                                "sense_id": "334be1c7-4ec7-3462-8ee6-0f63b218b18f",
                                                "text": "These bits were fill-ins between what had to be said to carry on life and work and they were constant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cff614d-daa1-447f-be20-fc2f0b602ebb",
                                                "sense_id": "334be1c7-4ec7-3462-8ee6-0f63b218b18f",
                                                "text": "There were all kinds of different tips with varying widths of sprays—fat and skinny ones with special names. Fats were for fill-ins, and skinny tips usually for the outlines, unless you used a fat cap for a tag and attempted to “flare” the ends of your letters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "523eb029-3254-43bb-be06-42203a253875",
                                                "sense_id": "334be1c7-4ec7-3462-8ee6-0f63b218b18f",
                                                "text": "Bess never understood why the corners of the foundation had to have these rounded fill-ins; they weren't load bearing and were plastered over."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3773db8e-4b50-42a0-9aab-e60ecc2d076f",
                                                "sense_id": "334be1c7-4ec7-3462-8ee6-0f63b218b18f",
                                                "text": "As we do not like knowledge gaps, we construct “fill-ins” to enable a coherent sense of the self and an awareness of others."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98597b85-d146-43bb-8a55-5231735ece2c",
                                                "sense_id": "334be1c7-4ec7-3462-8ee6-0f63b218b18f",
                                                "text": "Roadways became patchworks of asphalt fill-ins and forgotten cement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e20db65e-6633-39bc-a7d3-4a7d4e5b392f",
                                        "entry_id": "c77afaff-5d8e-3b7b-b7ce-0305752f0141",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something added to increase the size of something; padding or filler."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "925a2528-27da-449b-9049-13b22a959ff0",
                                                "sense_id": "e20db65e-6633-39bc-a7d3-4a7d4e5b392f",
                                                "text": "There was, at that time, a small film producing complex known as Ben Blake Studios where a variety of trailers, commercials, fill-ins, and (yes) screen tests were shot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3ac9125-e864-493e-a426-442227a91e65",
                                                "sense_id": "e20db65e-6633-39bc-a7d3-4a7d4e5b392f",
                                                "text": "It is not a gossipy yarn; nor is it a dry, monotonous account, full of such customary 'fill-ins' as 'romantic moonlight casting murky shadows down a long, winding country road'."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6e110cc-6e18-4350-aa27-a116c475720a",
                                                "sense_id": "e20db65e-6633-39bc-a7d3-4a7d4e5b392f",
                                                "text": "Thus a film like René Laloux's Fantastic Planet (1973) clearly involves human or humanlike characters—yet the mode of presentation eschews historical fill-ins, and many of the events are hallucinatory rather than realistic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "baa3cff9-6bb7-4991-a64c-2860886115af",
                                                "sense_id": "e20db65e-6633-39bc-a7d3-4a7d4e5b392f",
                                                "text": "When making these comparisons, we can clearly see many fill-ins throughout the stories. Most of them are incidental and have little bearing on the story; others are remarkably important."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3836cac2-8950-4852-8adb-041ca41659e5",
                                                "sense_id": "e20db65e-6633-39bc-a7d3-4a7d4e5b392f",
                                                "text": "As creators produced more material than might be published in a given month, a back stock of material would be accumulated, much of which could be used as fill-ins in cases when publishing schedules might run afoul."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f505f520-7754-31b2-abe2-4b3086e65473",
                                        "entry_id": "c77afaff-5d8e-3b7b-b7ce-0305752f0141",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A product category that is used to complete a range or variety of a product line."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d54fcfe-b69e-4373-8ecc-1657da4eb9df",
                                                "sense_id": "f505f520-7754-31b2-abe2-4b3086e65473",
                                                "text": "Since consumer buying behaviour to obtain staples is different from fill-ins, retailers strategy will also differ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b1a5d2c-992f-4f47-8ba4-3ee7748a6777",
                                                "sense_id": "f505f520-7754-31b2-abe2-4b3086e65473",
                                                "text": "Variety enhancers may have medium to high margins, while the fill-ins will have higher profit margins due to the longer time these items may need to move off the shelf in a retail store."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bcfe3e56-6a45-47d9-b277-21038c4d02a3",
                        "source_entry_id": "92aa9223-f515-3982-8f15-208493512a1d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b5d4657e-69ec-3d15-99a0-a85c18b43330",
                        "source_sense_description": "abwertend: Ersatz für etwas oder jemanden in Ermangelung einer besseren Alternative",
                        "target_lang_word": "expédient",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "expédient",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "13376f50-bbd5-3c81-965a-dbdb47c5e520",
                                        "entry_id": "04a036ca-4da9-3416-a5b9-0ecdaca9bc0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est utile, opportun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a7e78a3-d057-4c5e-962e-6a8ec5955f40",
                                                "sense_id": "13376f50-bbd5-3c81-965a-dbdb47c5e520",
                                                "text": "Il est expédient de faire cela, que vous fassiez cela."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "342495cd-fb65-4dcf-8253-56dd3bb67a6e",
                                                "sense_id": "13376f50-bbd5-3c81-965a-dbdb47c5e520",
                                                "text": "Cette terminaison à la réflexion me paraissait logique et bien expédiente."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd9176da-0c60-45d9-b448-6bc511163ea3",
                                                "sense_id": "13376f50-bbd5-3c81-965a-dbdb47c5e520",
                                                "text": "Entre le Christ, Calvin et M. le sénateur Bérenger, ce n’est que de la terrasse d’un café que la confusion est possible. Mais il peut être expédient de les fourrer dans le même sac."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "183fd51e-d79b-4a13-ae33-02ebc1c1193a",
                                                "sense_id": "13376f50-bbd5-3c81-965a-dbdb47c5e520",
                                                "text": "Il est expédient de bifurquer à faux pour dérouter les pillards qui braconnent les tenderies dès l'aube, avant le propriétaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1682644d-a39c-4d6b-b6dc-9bb02a667589",
                                                "sense_id": "13376f50-bbd5-3c81-965a-dbdb47c5e520",
                                                "text": "Vous ferez ce que vous jugerez expédient."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8718595-3b0c-4e85-9210-1b709e9bb634",
                                                "sense_id": "13376f50-bbd5-3c81-965a-dbdb47c5e520",
                                                "text": "Cela est expédient ou il est expédient, il est à propos, il est nécessaire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "expédient",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "139092a5-66a7-3037-a989-4b7b59e697de",
                                        "entry_id": "1290b4e8-9898-3026-acce-bde373f5f55d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Moyen de rencontre pour résoudre quelque difficulté, surmonter un obstacle, réussir dans quelque affaire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd267c0b-0646-4279-bc2e-e5e842cadcab",
                                                "sense_id": "139092a5-66a7-3037-a989-4b7b59e697de",
                                                "text": "Déroutés, les hommes du 24 mai cherchèrent une issue. On a dit qu'ils se rabattirent sur un expédient : la République sans les républicains. Ce n'est pas tout à fait cela. Ils essayèrent de fonder le mac-mahonisme qui, dans leur esprit devait préparer l'orléanisme."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d4d078c-331c-38c6-9148-2b6b6f92ae37",
                                        "entry_id": "1290b4e8-9898-3026-acce-bde373f5f55d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ressource passagère qui parfois ne libère que provisoirement d’un embarras."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7045c2d-5e6a-4392-9cfe-62ea1e74c908",
                                                "sense_id": "0d4d078c-331c-38c6-9148-2b6b6f92ae37",
                                                "text": "L'honorable M. Bertauld nous a dit encore : Je repousse votre projet de loi parce que c'est un expédient, une loi de circonstance, et qu'il n'appartient pas aux assemblées politiques de se saisir de faits particuliers pour en faire l'objet d'une modification législative."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "484a1bf9-c661-4e17-a2c2-ba47b8cfb370",
                                                "sense_id": "0d4d078c-331c-38c6-9148-2b6b6f92ae37",
                                                "text": "La faim me devenait intolérable et, dans quelques heures, c’était de nouveau la nuit ; il s’agissait de trouver un expédient pendant qu’il en était temps encore."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8f239b5-7773-4207-8ed8-86ad8fab8c59",
                                                "sense_id": "0d4d078c-331c-38c6-9148-2b6b6f92ae37",
                                                "text": "J'accepte toutes les commandes qui me rapportent, même les plus farfelues, là où la plupart d'entre eux ne s'engagent que dans des oeuvres nobles, quitte à vivre d'expédients."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8059071-f90f-48d8-b46d-b1743781bcd9",
                                                "sense_id": "0d4d078c-331c-38c6-9148-2b6b6f92ae37",
                                                "text": "Cela fait plus de 640 jours que la Belgique fonctionne sans véritable gouvernement fédéral. Depuis que le roi Philippe a accepté la démission du gouvernement Michel, le 21 décembre 2018, [c]e Pays vit d’expédients, de bois de rallonge, de bricolages à court terme, sans budget, sans perspective, sans plan de relance avec devant lui la plus grande crise économique depuis la Seconde Guerre Mondiale et une pandémie à gérer vaille que vaille."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfd409db-12bd-48b1-b056-517d89d502b5",
                                                "sense_id": "0d4d078c-331c-38c6-9148-2b6b6f92ae37",
                                                "text": "N'être qu’un expédient, n'être qu'une ressource passagère qui laissera bientôt retomber dans l’embarras celui qui l’emploie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80d1adfe-16a6-4288-924c-be673ab5110a",
                                                "sense_id": "0d4d078c-331c-38c6-9148-2b6b6f92ae37",
                                                "text": "Être aux expédients, en être aux expédients, être réduit à user de toutes sortes de moyens pour se procurer des ressources."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "expédient",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52b3d3e2-897b-3d20-9b73-fe3ac59b8abd",
                                        "entry_id": "575fa7b3-989a-3a37-b867-0fbda9e8793a",
